{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he said: The thing that you are doing is not good.</b> In my eyes, and he gave a reason for his words, namely נבול תבול, from the root of ועלהו לא יבול (Psalm 1:3), כאלה נובלת עליה (Isaiah 1:30), for the meaning is that he will fall of himself like a withered leaf, by way of parable, and the word גם is like it: גם כי כבד ממך הדבר (Exodus 18:18)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The phrase נבול תבול does not appear in the verse text of Exodus 18:17 in standard Masoretic text; Ibn Ezra appears to be reading it as an implied phrase or variant related to the root נבל 'to wither.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:38.592425913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}